    "answer": {
      "short": "$3:13$. After removal, cordial is $3.6\\div4=0.9$ L; final water is $4.8-0.9=3.9$ L.",
      "worked": "Removing mixture preserves the ratio $1:3$ in the liquid remaining.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Mixture remaining}&=4.8-1.2=3.6\\text{ L}\\\\4\\text{ parts}&=3.6\\text{ L}\\\\1\\text{ part}&=3.6\\div4=0.9\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Cordial remaining}&=0.9\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Water remaining}&=3\\times0.9=2.7\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Final water}&=2.7+1.2=3.9\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Cordial}:\\text{water}&=0.9:3.9=9:39=3:13\\end{align*}$$",
